	(text "Link USB-C port per spec §6. Variants: 'upstream' (default population; right upstream, numpad) and 'downstream' (left, right downstream).\nUpstream: KTS1693 with external OVLO 100k / 26.4k 0.1 % (trip 5.55-5.95 V); ISET 4.99k -> OCP 1.82-2.18 A latch-off\n(datasheet rev 04d Table 1; was 1M, no OCP, until E9 2026-09-15); EN and OC_MODE low; ACOK open-drain to J_LB pin 5, pulled up on the core (wired-OR on right).\nDownstream: U601, R601-R603 and J_LB not fitted; R604 0 ohm 1206 (CRCW1206 jumper 3.5 A, <=20 mOhm) bridges VBUS; J_LBD fitted, no ACOK.\nR604 must never be fitted with U601: it bypasses the OVP. Upstream: U603, C603, R605 and J_LBD not fitted.\nDownstream U603 TPS22950L (P14) switches J_LBD VBUS to VBUS_CONN (port, J_SEAM; via R604 to C602/D601), ON = LINK_SW_EN (J_LBD 6, smart pulldown; series R on the core).\nR605 624 ohm (SLVSFJ2B Table 7.5): latches off above IHCD 1.2-1.9 A for 120-188 us, peak 2.1 A typ; <=2 A for 2 J_LBD contacts (P9).\nCleared only by toggling ON or VIN. No reverse current blocking (SLVSFJ2B Table 5). FLT not used. CIN 1 uF per SLVSFJ2B 10.3.\nNo CC resistors: a charger never enables VBUS into a link port. A6=B6 (LA) and A7=B7 (LB) tied; A8 (S1) and B8 (S2) separate.\nTPD6E05U06 on all six signal pins, at the receptacle. J_SEAM joins the seam board ahead of the KTS1693.\nJ_SEAM, J_LB, J_LBD are reversal-safe: pin k and N+1-k never pair VBUS with GND; LA/LB swap with S2/S1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 10.16 193.04 0.0000)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			) (justify left top)
		)
